      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. documentation seems like the best way to keep it clean. \n\none last thing though—the client mentioned something about \"trade secrets\" being separate from \"confidential information\" in another part of the doc. is there a big difference in how the residuals clause applies to those? like, if i remember a trade secret in my 'unaided memory', am i still protected by this residuals section or does the trade secret status override that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
